{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455645-autumn-changeling-chronicle","id":1455645,"title":"Autumn Changeling Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-27T00:33:30-07:00","id":1455645,"title":"Autumn Changeling Chronicle","content":"I am planning an Autumn court focused Changeling Chronicle that reuses several characters from my Epic Changeling Chronicle, liked Edgar Allen Poe. I have used to Edgar Allen Poe to explore many of our modern holidays to old pagan rituals. In my chronicle, he acts the role of Carapace Clavicle Moundshroud from The Halloween Tree by guilding the motely through the Hedge and Arcadia, even the underworld, while teaching them the history Samhain and Walpurgis Night, and also touching upon old horror stories like The Legend of Sleepy Hollow, The Tailypo, and Jack o' the Lantern . Because the 2e Author Kith hasn\u2019t been revealed yet, Edgar Allen Poe does not use his fae magic directly. He provides them with the tools and hints they need to overcome their struggles, BUT never directly helps them by fighting the True Fae for them. Note: It is his wife Eliza (called Anabell Lee) who convinces him to help the character. Though her husband his difficulty emphasizing with humans and even low wyrd changelings, Annabell still possesses strong empathy for humanity. I want to reuse him again to explore the horror stories and pagan rituals connected to Autumn, but plan to use other characters, as well. I have decided to bring in Ichabod Crane as an Antiquarian Darkling and one of Edgar Allen Poe's few true friends. I plan to introduce the Dullahan/Headless Horeman as the stories huntsmen. Does anyone have suggestion for other fairytale characters they might bring in? If so, why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T11:53:44-07:00","id":1455674,"title":"","content":"Three other characters I am thinking of putting in the chronicle as members of the Autumn Court are <i><b>Hansel </b></i>and <i><b>Gretel,</b></i> and <i><b>Little Red Riding Hood</b></i>. I am thinking of making Hansel an Ogre Gristlegrinder, Gretel as a Witchtooth Darkling, and Little Red Riding Hood as a Beast Hunterheart. I am curious as to whether you agree with making them members of the Autumn Court and ideas for playing their personalities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T12:53:24-07:00","id":1455677,"title":"","content":"Jack of the Lantern is one of my favorite Halloween figures to use - and can definitely emphasize the Autumn Court\u2019s themes twisting around the Fae\u2019s words to overcome them, as well as turning a Curse into power, the burden of isolation, and trying to use people\u2019s fear of you to help them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what setting or cultural backgrounds your drawing on, but Poe makes me think of 19th Century New England\u2026 and for some reason that made me think of Jeffery Donner as a mythic Autumn Court figure. While his story happens in winter, I\u2019d argue it resonates a lot more with fear. The movie \u2018Ravenous\u2019 would be my recommendation for inspiration.<br /> <br /> And if that\u2019s a setting you\u2019re drawing on, using someone from the Salem witch trials would also make a strong character. Perhaps the prosecutor as a Huntsman, or one of the accused as a Hedge Ghost. The trials might also be interesting to use as a cover for a loyalist plot and/or hunt - the echoes of which might still have lingering consequences, and characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 07-27-2021, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T15:26:26-07:00","id":1455680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455645-autumn-changeling-chronicle?p=1455677#post1455677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jack of the Lantern is one of my favorite Halloween figures to use - and can definitely emphasize the Autumn Court\u2019s themes twisting around the Fae\u2019s words to overcome them, as well as turning a Curse into power, the burden of isolation, and trying to use people\u2019s fear of you to help them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what setting or cultural backgrounds your drawing on, but Poe makes me think of 19th Century New England\u2026 and for some reason that made me think of Jeffery Donner as a mythic Autumn Court figure. While his story happens in winter, I\u2019d argue it resonates a lot more with fear. The movie \u2018Ravenous\u2019 would be my recommendation for inspiration.<br /> <br /> And if that\u2019s a setting you\u2019re drawing on, using someone from the Salem witch trials would also make a strong character. Perhaps the prosecutor as a Huntsman, or one of the accused as a Hedge Ghost. The trials might also be interesting to use as a cover for a loyalist plot and/or hunt - the echoes of which might still have lingering consequences, and characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do plan to use Jack O the Lantern and make him a character Edgar Allen Poe detests. I plan to have the story <i>At LEAST START</i> in modern times. One of the books I am using for inspiration is the <b><i>Halloween Tree</i></b>, so I might include time travel in the story. I also plan to do some globe hopping. I want to story to emphasize ALL the themes associated with Autumn; not just fear, but also air, ghosts, spirits, the occult, witchcraft, endings, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T15:54:29-07:00","id":1455682,"title":"","content":"P.S. What Seeming and Kith would you make Jack o the Lantern? In 1e Grimm fears, he was a Wizened Chatelaine, but I think he makes a better darkling. On the other hand, I already have several darklings and would like to use other seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T22:21:46-07:00","id":1455701,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t played changeling in 2E, so I don\u2019t have in in depth reading on that part, but off the top of my head a Cleverquick (Dark Eras 2), probably as a Darkling, is how I would stay him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T23:58:44-07:00","id":1455705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455645-autumn-changeling-chronicle?p=1455701#post1455701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven\u2019t played changeling in 2E, so I don\u2019t have in in depth reading on that part, but off the top of my head a Cleverquick (Dark Eras 2), probably as a Darkling, is how I would stay him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't a Cleverquick a Kith distinct to the plains indians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T10:12:06-07:00","id":1455717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455645-autumn-changeling-chronicle?p=1455705#post1455705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't a Cleverquick a Kith distinct to the plains indians?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ach, I knew there was going to be a detail I forgot. Like I said, I haven\u2019t done much with Changeling 2E yet. <br /> If you didn\u2019t mind spending some time on conversion, Whisperwisp, Larcenist, or Gravewright are probably the 1E Kiths I\u2019d suggest","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T11:24:06-07:00","id":1455723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455645-autumn-changeling-chronicle?p=1455717#post1455717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ach, I knew there was going to be a detail I forgot. Like I said, I haven\u2019t done much with Changeling 2E yet.<br /> If you didn\u2019t mind spending some time on conversion, Whisperwisp, Larcenist, or Gravewright are probably the 1E Kiths I\u2019d suggest</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or perhaps a smith, because Jack was originally a blacksmith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T13:40:01-07:00","id":1455729,"title":"","content":"I am trying to build the backgrounds and personalities of Hansel and Gretel. Right now, I think they are enforces of the Autumn court in Germany. Does anyone have any advice/suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T21:28:45-07:00","id":1455783,"title":"","content":"For inspiration on the Autumn Court, I am watching <i>Tim Burton's </i><b><i>The Nightmare Before Christmas, </i></b> <i><b>Hocus Pocus, </b></i> and the 2008 movie, <i><b>Trick or Treat</b></i>. Does Anyone have any other suggestions for sources?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T22:21:03-07:00","id":1455784,"title":"","content":"You have great taste <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26937-todoqanu","name":"todoqanu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T22:39:08-07:00","id":1455786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>todoqanu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455645-autumn-changeling-chronicle?p=1455784#post1455784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have great taste <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Do you have any suggestions for the high wyrd changeling characters I mentioned above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T21:20:21-07:00","id":1456331,"title":"","content":"I thought I would describe Anna Belle Lee a bit more as she is an important character in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> Anna Belle Lee (Virginia Eliza Clemm Poe) is an important character in the previous chronicle, because she was the one who convinces her husband to help the characters. Even as an ordinary mortal, Edgar Allan Poe was an outcast and eccentric among society. These qualities became worse after becoming a changeling and living beyond the mortal lifespan. While not as causally cruel as the True Fae, HE IS very manipulative with other characters and the only person he truly cares about is his wife. Anna Belle, on the other hand still possess a great deal of empathy and sympathy for humanity and changelings who come from the current era. While she does love him, she will work against her husband, if she feels what he is doing is wrong.<br /> <br /> Right now, she is a Fairest Nymph, though this might change is we are introduced to another water kith in the Kith and Kin book. For mortals who see only her mask, she is a beautiful southern belle in her early twenties with flame red hair and spring leaf green eyes. Behind the mask, her skin is fresh water blue, with her eyes and hair salt water green. Her hands are webbed and she can turn her legs into fins when she wants to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T21:25:34-07:00","id":1456333,"title":"","content":"Here is a description of Edgar Allen Poe's mien.<br /> <br /> Mien: Poe\u2019s mien is 8 feet tall with inhumanly long digits and limbs. His skin is jet black and his eyes glow like a jack o\u2019 lantern. His ears are large pointed and catlike, though his face somewhat resembles a ravens.<br /> <br /> These alien features are hidden behind his mask. Because his face is so well known, he has the many mask merit and has created multiple identities for himself in the mortal world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}